# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked into
# the published image.

# data/ holds the live SQLite database. Copying it in would ship whatever was
# on the build machine and then have it shadowed by the volume mount at
# runtime -- wrong either way, and it puts real stock data in a registry.
data/

# Built on the host, for the host. The image runs its own `uv sync`.
.venv/

# Secrets, by the same argument as data/. `*.env` matters as much as `.env`:
# a production.env kept in the tree would otherwise be published in the image,
# and it holds SECRET_KEY.
.env
*.env
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
staticfiles/
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
.DS_Store

# Documentation and editor state: no effect on the running app, but every
# change to them would otherwise invalidate the COPY layer and its rebuild.
*.md
.claude/
